node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store

# Locally reproducible replay output stays untracked.
benchmark/results/*
# Measured visual results ARE the evidence a review depends on, so they are
# versioned. Scope the exception to the visual result files only: everything
# else under benchmark/results (local replays, ad-hoc runs) stays ignored.
!benchmark/results/visual-*.json
*.tgz

# Local live-campaign runner: reads an operator-provided key file, never committed.
live-jev-runner.mjs

# Provider evidence under `benchmark/evidence/` is committed ON PURPOSE: it is
# the dated record a review depends on, and it cannot be re-derived without
# spending a provider call.
#
# The policy, in terms:
#
# - a committed report keeps its per-case OBSERVATIONS (probabilities,
#   confidences, gate values), because those ARE the evidence;
# - a committed report must never carry a raw endpoint, key, header or private
#   path — `test/conformance-campaign.test.ts` fails the build if one does;
# - if a report starts carrying source or session content rather than public
#   fixture text, it must be reduced, not committed as-is. See
#   docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md for the number-only rule that applies to the
#   smaller campaign snapshots.
#
# Anything regenerable stays ignored: that is `benchmark/results/`, above.
#
# NOTE: this directory is deliberately NOT excluded. A rule of `**` here was
# briefly present and silently untracked every provider run, while the comment
# above claimed the opposite — the evidence a review depends on was absent from
# the repository, and a contract test failed only because a file was missing.
